              with a base point adjoined. That however is isomorphic to the unreduced mapping cone of the original inclusion. With this the natural isomorphism is given by lemma
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EvaluationOfCohomologyTheoryOnGoodPairIsEvaluationOnQuotient"}
            %p The other composite is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mover
                                %mi E
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                              %mo •
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
