          %p Finally we record the following basic relation between reduced and unreduced cohomology:
          #UnreducedCohomologyIsReducedPlusPointValue.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^\bullet
              be an unreduced cohomology theory, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E^\bullet
              its reduced cohomology theory from def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FromUnreducedToReducedCohomology"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\ast)
              a pointed topological space, then there is an identification
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^\bullet(X) \simeq \tilde E^\bullet(X) \oplus E^\bullet(\ast)
            %p
              of the unreduced cohomology of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
              of the reduced cohomology of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
