                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    composite of this
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+implication"} linear implication
                    with daggered-counit followed by unit
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+transform"} integral transform
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+quantization"}> motivic
                    \/cohomological
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trace"} trace
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler+characteristic"} Euler characteristic
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
          %h2#references References
          %p The original article on the Eilenberg–Steenrod axioms:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Eilenberg"}> Samuel Eilenberg
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Norman+E.+Steenrod"} Norman E. Steenrod
              = succeed "," do
                %em Axiomatic Approach to Homology Theory
              %strong 31
              4 (1945) 117–120 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1073/pnas.31.4.117"}> doi:10.1073/pnas.31.4.117
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Further development and an expository account:
          %ul
            %li#EilenbergSteenrod52
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Eilenberg"}> Samuel Eilenberg
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Norman+Steenrod"} Norman Steenrod
              = succeed "," do
                %em Foundations of algebraic topology
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/eilestee.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/books/hardcover/9780691653297/foundations-of-algebraic-topology"} ISBN:9780691653297
          %p
            The concept of generalized homology obtained by discarding the dimension axiom and the observation that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            induces an example is due to
          %ul
            %li#Whitehead62
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/George+Whitehead"}> George Whitehead
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Generalized homology theories
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/s0002-9947-1962-0137117-6"} doi
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1993676"} jstor:1993676
          %p
            The proof that every generalized (co)homology theory arises this way (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"}> Brown representability theorem
            ) is due to
          %ul
            %li#Brown62
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edgar+Brown"}> Edgar Brown
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cohomology theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/1970209"} jstor:1970209
            %li#Brown65
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edgar+Brown"}> Edgar Brown
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Abstract homotopy theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/S0002-9947-1965-0182970-6"} doi:10.1090/S0002-9947-1965-0182970-6
          %p
            Earlu discussion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Atiyah-Hirzebruch+spectral+sequence"} Atiyah-Hirzebruch spectral sequence
            in this generality (and use of the terminology “extraordinary cohomology”):
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C.+R.+F.+Maunder"}> C. R. F. Maunder
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em The spectral sequence of an extraordinary cohomology theory
              %strong 59
              3 (1963) 567-574 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100037245"}> doi:10.1017/S0305004100037245
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Early lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li#Adams74
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
              , part III, sections 2 and 6 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalised+homology"} Stable homotopy and generalised homology
              (1974)
          %p Monographs:
          %ul
            %li#Switzer75
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Switzer"}> Robert Switzer
                , chapter 7 (and 8-12) of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic Topology - Homotopy and Homology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Michael+Boardman"}> John Michael Boardman
                , Section 3 of:
                %em Stable Operations in Generalized Cohomology
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://math.jhu.edu/~wsw/papers2/math/28a-boardman-stable.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Boardman-StableOperations.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ioan+Mackenzie+James"} Ioan Mackenzie James
                (ed.)
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Algebraic+Topology"} Handbook of Algebraic Topology
                Oxford 1995 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-0-444-81779-2.X5000-7"}> doi:10.1016/B978-0-444-81779-2.X5000-7
                )
            %li#Kochman96
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Kochman"}> Stanley Kochman
                , section 3.4 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bordism%2C+Stable+Homotopy+and+Adams+Spectral+Sequences"} Bordism, Stable Homotopy and Adams Spectral Sequences
            %li#May99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+May"} Peter May
                chapter 18 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Concise Course on Algebraic Topology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/CONCISE/ConciseRevised.pdf"} pdf
            %li#AguilarGitlerPrieto02
              %p
                Marcelo Aguilar,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Gitler"} Samuel Gitler
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic topology from a homotopical viewpoint
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://tocs.ulb.tu-darmstadt.de/106999419.pdf"} toc pdf
            %li#KonoTamaki02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akira+Kono"}> Akira Kono
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dai+Tamaki"} Dai Tamaki
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalized cohomology
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GeneralizedCohomology.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/mmono-230"} ISBN: 978-0-8218-3514-2
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
                , chapter II, section 6 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Symmetric+spectra"} Symmetric spectra
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/~schwede/SymSpec-v3.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in the further generality of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+cohomology"} equivariant cohomology
            is in
          %ul
            %li#tomDieck79
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tammo+tom+Dieck"}> Tammo tom Dieck
              , section 7 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Transformation+Groups+and+Representation+Theory"} Transformation Groups and Representation Theory
          %p
            A pedagogical introduction to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectra
            and generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              %a{:href => "http://math.ucr.edu/home/baez/twf_ascii/week149"} TWF 149
          %p
            Formulation in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+theory"} (infinity,1)-category theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#LurieHigherAlgebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , section 1.4.1 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"} Higher Algebra
          %p
            More references relating to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"} nPOV
            on cohomology include:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"}> Mike Hopkins
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Complex+oriented+cohomology+theories+and+the+language+of+stacks"} Complex oriented cohomology theories and the language of stacks
                course notes (
                %a{:href => "https://web.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/otherpapers/coctalos.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology+-+cohomology+theories"} A Survey of Elliptic Cohomology - cohomology theories
          %p
            Formulation in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            (cf.
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+in+homotopy+type+theory"} cohomology in homotopy type theory
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Evan+Cavallo"}> Evan Cavallo
                , Section 3.2 of:
                %em Synthetic Cohomology in Homotopy Type Theory
                (2015) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://staff.math.su.se/evan.cavallo/works/thesis15.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Cavallo-CohomologyInHoTT.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Floris+van+Doorn"}> Floris van Doorn
                , around Def. 5.4.2 in:
                %em On the Formalization of Higher Inductive Types and Synthetic Homotopy Theory
                (2018) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1808.10690"}> arXiv:1808.10690
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://florisvandoorn.com/papers/dissertation.pdf"} pdf
        .revisedby
